# Component workflow

## Edit the component, not the instance

When asked to change something, change the **component**, so every instance
across the site changes with it — even when the request names a specific page
("the services rows on /about", "the grid on the homepage"). Only scope a change
to one page when explicitly told to.

If a request genuinely needs to differ per page, add a prop to the single
component rather than forking it into a second one.

## Always update the design system page

`src/app/design-system/page.tsx` is the catalogue. Every component change must
update it in the same pass:

1. **Render it** — new components go in `SECTION_PREVIEWS` (section components)
   or the atoms group, so Cursor design mode can edit them.
2. **Rewrite the description** if behaviour changed. A note that describes
   removed behaviour is worse than no note. Mention props and any layout
   constraints a consumer has to respect.
3. **Remove the entry** when a component is deleted.

"Used on:" lines are derived automatically from the import graph by
`src/lib/component-usage.ts` — never hand-maintain them.

Verify coverage after any add/remove:

```sh
find src/components -name "*.tsx" -exec rg -o 'export function ([A-Za-z]+)' -r '$1' {} \; | sort -u
rg -o '(?:name: "|  )([A-Z][A-Za-z]+)(?:",| ?: <)' -r '$1' src/app/design-system/page.tsx --pcre2 | sort -u
```

## No dead code

Deleting a component means deleting its file, its imports, its design-system
entry, and any content fields only it consumed.
